DMA record: horizontal display-window events land at the clock they happen

decide_hdiw_check_start() records DMA_EVENT_HDIWS twice and decide_hdiw_check_stop() records
DMA_EVENT_HDIWE once, all through diw_to_hpos(), which converts a Denise position in shres
units (8 per colour clock) to an Agnus hpos. The first HDIWS passes val, which is in those
units. The second HDIWS and the HDIWE pass first/last instead: coord_diw_shres_to_window_x()
of val, a window x in the OUTPUT resolution. Only a super-hires frame has shres window units,
so on the usual hires frame every horizontal DIW event was recorded at about half its clock.

Seen in Peekaboo's raster overlay on an OCS A500 at hires, DIWSTRT $3491 / DIWSTOP $FCC1: the
record put HDIWS at hpos 40 and HDIWE at 116 on every display line, where the window opens at
Denise clock 72.5 and closes at 224.5 (hpos 76 and 228 once diw_to_hpos() adds its 4 clocks).
The "Per-line DDF/DIW" layer drew its display-window marks at those wrong clocks, while the DDF
marks next to them (recorded in hpos directly) were right.

Both now pass val. Only the debugger's record changes; drawing uses first/last as before.

Applies to libretro-uae 2b0ed42fe565fb997a0627aaa8f44e0948b527f8 in the order given by
patches/series.txt.

--- a/sources/src/custom.c
+++ b/sources/src/custom.c
@@ -1663,7 +1663,9 @@ static void decide_hdiw_check_start(int start_diw_hpos, int end_diw_hpos)
 				}
 #ifdef DEBUGGER
 				if (debug_dma) {
-					record_dma_event(DMA_EVENT_HDIWS, diw_to_hpos(first), vpos);
+					// ADM: val, not first - diw_to_hpos() takes Denise shres units, and first is
+					// a window x in the output resolution (right only for a super-hires frame).
+					record_dma_event(DMA_EVENT_HDIWS, diw_to_hpos(val), vpos);
 				}
 #endif
 			}
@@ -1692,7 +1694,8 @@ static void decide_hdiw_check_stop(int start_diw_hpos, int end_diw_hpos)
 				last_diwlastword = val;
 #ifdef DEBUGGER
 				if (debug_dma) {
-					record_dma_event(DMA_EVENT_HDIWE, diw_to_hpos(last), vpos);
+					// ADM: val, not last - see DMA_EVENT_HDIWS above.
+					record_dma_event(DMA_EVENT_HDIWE, diw_to_hpos(val), vpos);
 				}
 #endif
 			}
